# JobReady — Frontend Developer Journey

A simple app to prepare for your next frontend developer role.

## What is inside?
- 21 small HTML, CSS, JavaScript, quality, Git, and career practice steps.
- Portfolio, task manager, and expense tracker project checklists.
- Interview questions with prepared example answers.
- Job application tracker.
- Progress backup download and restore.

## Try it on your computer
1. Extract this ZIP (on Windows, right-click it and choose Extract All).
2. Open index.html in Chrome or Edge.
3. Open Learning path and start with Step 01.

No installation or build command is needed.

## Upload to GitHub and get a website link
1. Sign in to GitHub and create a new public repository named jobready.
2. In the repository, choose Add file > Upload files (or the upload files link in an empty repository).
3. Upload the EXTRACTED index.html, app.js, and README.md into the main level of the repository. Do not upload the ZIP as your website, or put index.html inside another folder.
4. Click Commit changes.
5. Open Settings > Pages.
6. Under Build and deployment, set Source to Deploy from a branch.
7. Choose main and / (root), then click Save.
8. When publishing finishes, return to Settings > Pages and open the website link shown there.

Typical address: https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/jobready/
Replace YOUR-USERNAME with your actual GitHub username.

Official instructions:
https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/configuring-a-publishing-source-for-your-github-pages-site

## How to use it
- Learning path: read a step, try the task in your own code editor, then mark it complete.
- My projects: build your own projects and tick the working features. Add project links.
- Interview practice: write an answer, then reveal the example.
- Job tracker: add a company and role, then update status and next step.
- My dashboard: download a progress backup before switching devices or browsers.

## Your data
Progress saves in localStorage in your current browser. It does not automatically sync across devices. The GitHub Pages version has a different website address from the original version, so use Download my progress and Restore backup to transfer existing data if you have access to the original version.

This app provides prepared practice content, not AI grading or a guarantee of employment.

## Edit the app
index.html contains the layout and CSS styles.
app.js contains the learning content, interview examples, and app behavior.
Keep both files together. There are no external dependencies or private hosting requirements.
